    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `fill_gaps` in `app/gaps.py`, and all 6 tests pass (the 2 existing ones plus 4 new ones in `tests/test_gaps.py`).\n\n**How it works:**\n- It works on a copy of the input, so the original frame is never changed.\n- It groups `temp_c` by `station`. Each gap is filled from the station's own values: first the most recent earlier reading, then, if there isn't one, the first later reading.\n- Only missing values are filled; existing temperatures are never touched. A station with no temperatures at all keeps its missing values.\n- Rows come back in the same order with the same index, and `station`, `ts` and `battery` are unchanged.\n- Rows are matched by position, not by index label, so a repeated or out-of-order index can't make values land on the wrong row.\n\n**One case your spec didn't cover:** if a row has no `station` value, I leave its temperature as it is. I don't lump all station-less rows together, since they may come from different stations.\n\n**New tests** cover: filling only within a station (including a station with no data and a row with no station), unchanged row order and other columns, the input not being modified, and the nullable `Float64` column type being kept.\n\nThe project notes ask me to look up library docs through Context7, but its monthly quota had run out. I checked how pandas 3.0.6 behaves by running the tests instead."
